But is that acceptable/minimal? It exposes internals via app.locals — harmless, doesn't break anything. Alternatively, keep the DB open: better-sqlite3 allows multiple connections to same file; reopening while the first is open still works for reads (the second connection sees committed data). For the smoke earlier, I opened two connections simultaneously and it worked. So "feche" is nice-to-have; even without closing, reopen works because data was committed on insert. Actually the smoke earlier opened a2 while a1 was still open and read fine. SQLite with two connections: a1 inserted (committed), a2 reads fresh data. Works.

