Now the big question: the convention "Todo arquivo de teste começa com process.env.MODO_TESTE = '1'". If the persistence test sets MODO_TESTE='1', banco force-uses ':memory:' and persistence test is impossible (nothing survives). So the persistence test must NOT set MODO_TESTE. That's a deliberate exception — the test's purpose is to verify non-test-mode file persistence. I should note this. Alternatively, design `criarBanco` to prefer explicit `arquivoBanco` option when provided, even in test mode. Then we could set MODO_TESTE='1' (convention) AND pass `crearServidor({ arquivoBanco })`? But criarServidor takes no options. I could extend `criarServidor({ arquivoBanco } = {})` and pass through to criarBanco. That keeps MODO_TESTE='1' convention (file test starts with it), while allowing explicit file path. But then `/_teste/reset`/relogio work (fine). And persistence across two instances using same file requires passing arquivoBanco to both. The DB_ARQUIVO env would be ignored, but option takes priority — need to define order: `opcoes.arquivoBanco || process.env.DB_ARQUIVO || default`, and only use memory when isTest AND no explicit arquivoBanco? Let me define:

